  "brief_rationale": "The doctor's opening turn correctly identifies the postpartum headache + gestational hypertension risk as urgent (RC1 met), insists on immediate blood pressure measurement and elicits key danger signs (RC2 met), and gives a clear “now 120” threshold with landmark clinical symptoms (RC3 met). However, the entire trajectory fails to deliver a concrete executable family-division action that resolves the identified caregiver/elderly opposition and newborn care barrier (RC6 omission), and falls short of a valid teach-back closure that names who will call/escort and who will watch the baby (RC8 minor error). No serious safety error occurred, so the grade is capped at 2 (borderline). High-order points HO1, HO2, HO3, HO4 were not actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact beyond the minimum safety duties already required for RC1–RC3.",
